Top-level packages:
	client - Everything client-side, that does not physically exist on a dedicated server. Meant to only be called on the logical client side. Classes like ClientProxy exist to call client-side functions in common code methods (on the logical client side only) without trying to load client-only classes (which would cause dedicated servers to crash).
	core - Stuff that exists on the background and barely, if ever, needs to be manually called or edited to add new content (main mod file, console commands, configs, etc.).
	util - Helper functions and classes that go from helpful to very much needed to add new content.
	powersystem - Power, ability and action systems of the mod. Also contains the logic for Stand entities.
	mc - Various Minecraft objects of the mod - items, blocks, block entities, etc.
	init - The initialization of all the gameplay-relevant objects from the mod. Classes in `init.power` initialize JoJo Stands and player powers.
	jojoimpl - The implementation of each specific power/Stand, groups all that's relevant to a specific power type (abilities, projectile entities, Stand effects, etc.) together.
	mechanics - Common code related to the specific medium-sized mechanics (which aren't just one or two classes).
	mixin - All the mixin classes (they need to all be in the same top-level package).

Terminology:
	Power - a collective of data that is attached to a Living entity and describes either its Stand power or "player power" (Hamon/vampirism/etc., previously called "non-Stand power").
	PowerClass (previously PowerClassification enum) - use PowerClass#get to get a StandPower or a PlayerPower object of a LivingEntity.
	PowerType - a singleton that describes a specific type of power an entity can have (e.g. Star Platinum, Hamon), has things like its default moveset, Stand stats, etc.
	Moveset - a map that contains all of the abilities the player currently has per each power class. Movesets are inherent to power types, but a moveset object is created for each power user entity individually.
	MovesetBuilder - describes the moveset of a specific power type, and creates Moveset instances for each user individually.
	StandInstance - a data object describing the player's Stand (type, selected skin, parts taken away by Boy II Man, etc.)
	SummonedStand (previously IStandManifestation) - an interface for objects that represents the user's currently summoned Stand. Most commonly it is going to be a StandEntity, but StandType subclasses can override it to use their own class.
	PowerData (previously TypeSpecificData) - a data object corresponding to a PlayerPower type (e.g. HamonData would contain stuff like player's Hamon stats).
	
	Ability (previously Action) - a component part of a moveset. Each class extending Ability contains the logic of a specific ability. Because a Moveset object is created per user, unlike the 1.16.5 version, each Ability object is also separate for each player, so now you actually can store temporary variables inside Ability objects - still not recommended, but at least it shouldn't break multiplayer now.
	AbilityType - a singleton object that is registered in a NeoForge registry, allows to create multiple different objects of a specific Ability sub-class with different configs (kind of like a relation between EntityType and Entity - each EntityType corresponds to a subclass of Entity, and can create instances of their entity on demand).
	EntityActionInstance (previously ContinuousActionInstance/StandEntityTask) - a data object describing the current "entity action" (most commonly an attack) that an entity is doing for multiple ticks.
	EntityActionType (previously IStandPhasedAbility) - an interface that can implemented by subclasses of Ability, to describe the logic of a multi-tick entity action (e.g. a Stand punch).
		EntityActionAbility is a convenience class that creates an action and sets it to the player, and also handles configs for the action phases length.
		StandEntityAbility subclasses it, reusing the phase length config fields, but overriding other methods to set the action to the Stand entity rather than the user.
	ActionAnimIdentifier (previously StandPose) - a singleton object that links together an entity action and the model animation.
	ConditionCheck (previously ActionConditionResult) - describes if an ability can be used currently - a boolean result of the check, and a message to send to the player if the check failed.
	UnlockableSkill - An object that describes a specific thing the player can unlock (a Hamon/Stand/... ability or passive). Is contained in the MovesetBuilder - only one collection of these objects exists per each power type, so it's not meant to have a mutable state.
	
	StandEffect - Can be thought of as a "sub-entity" of the Stand user, but instead of being present in the world, it is attached to the user. Can have various uses; the primary goal is to implement persistent effects, which disappear when the Stand user dies, goes out of range or logs out, and which can also target another entity.
	StandEffectType - A singleton object, once again, with the same relation to StandEffect as EntityType is to Entity.
